09_01_2026 Module 2 Notes

Syntax, set of rules that define how code is written and structured
    - Syntax errors caught at compile

Primitive data types
    - Built in data types that store single values
    - Fast allocation, stored in stack
    - int
    - long
    - double
    - char

Categories
    - Numeric
        - Float, 6-7 decimals
        - Double, 15-16 decimals
        - bytes
        - short
        - int
        - long
    - Non-Numeric
        - char
        - boolean

To study: hexadecimal

Boolean defaults to false

Reference Data Types
    - Store a reference to objects in heap memory
    - Multiple references can point to the same object

Clearing reference = set reference to null
    - data = null

Type Conversion
    - Implicit Conversion and Explicit Conversion
    Implicit
        - Easy to convert to a larger data type
    Explicit
        - Convert larger to smaller
        - Possible data loss
        Casting syntax
            double d = 9.78;
            int i = (int) d;


Relational Operators
    - Always compares left to right
    - == can't be used on string since they're comparing addresses in memory, need to use .equals method instead
    - name1.equals(name2) returns a boolean



